  "weightScale": {
    "critical": 1.0,
    "normal": 0.7,
    "note": "Assumed by the expected outcomes in scenarios 02 to 10. The matcher owns the real values; if normal is not about 0.7, re-check scenario 06."
  },
  "matcherAssumptions": [
    "Removed identifiers are identifier-like tokens (containing _ . or -, or camelCase) found on '-' lines and NOT on '+' lines of the same change record. Plain words and ALL-CAPS words without _ (SQL keywords, COUNT) are not identifiers. Counting every '-' line token instead adds 6 false positives in scenario 10 and 4 in scenario 01, mostly through the token payments-api.",
    "Identifier matching against page text is whole-token, not substring.",
    "Snippet hash compares trimmed, whitespace-collapsed '-' lines of 5+ characters against page code block lines.",
    "Glob anchors never count as 'anchored file removed or renamed' for the High rule; exact path anchors do.",
    "Jira rule scores are multiplied by anchor weight, so Jira anchors meant to alert alone are critical."
  ],
